representation of a function,

00:27:11.940 --> 00:27:12.440
right?

00:27:12.440 --> 00:27:13.250
So you don't--

00:27:13.250 --> 00:27:14.870
BRENDAN JUBA: Well, yeah.

00:27:14.870 --> 00:27:17.120
So it's not going to tell
you much about the synthesis

00:27:17.120 --> 00:27:20.160
problem, because the vast--

00:27:20.160 --> 00:27:22.390
assuming that it's not unique--

00:27:22.390 --> 00:27:25.620
and if it's unique, it's
actually an easy problem.

00:27:25.620 --> 00:27:29.460
But assuming that it's not
unique or extremely not unique,

00:27:29.460 --> 00:27:31.080
then yeah, most
of these instances

00:27:31.080 --> 00:27:34.944
are just not things
that you can write down.

00:27:34.944 --> 00:27:39.220
So most of them are completely
irrelevant from the standpoint

00:27:39.220 --> 00:27:41.640
of efficient synthesis.

00:27:46.607 --> 00:27:48.190
MODERATOR: I'll keep
